    "chunk_text": "ACME Printing and Packaging shares up 3.33 percent as deal with Singer (Sri Lanka) takes shape\n\nSinger (Sri Lanka) has entered into a sale and purchase agreement with ACME Printing and Packaging to buy its factory in Piliyandala for Rs 630 million.\n\nThe move is \u201cpart of the restructuring of the Company and the expansion of the factory premises at Pannala,\u201d ACME said in a market disclosure, CSE sources said.\n\nThe factory is situated at 345, at Gonamadiththa Road, Piliyandala.\n\nShares of ACME Printing and Packaging were trading at Rs.6.20, up 3.33 percent. Singer shares were up 60 cents at Rs 87.50.\n\nAmid those developments, CSE yesterday kicked off on a positive note following a Janashakthi IPO.\n\nTherefore both indices showed an upward trend. All Share Price Index went up by 17.94 points while S and P SL20 rose by 3.72 points.\n\nTurnover stood at Rs 3.72 billion with seven crossings. Those crossings were; Digital Solutions 1.1 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 172.4 million; its shares traded at Rs 152, Prime Lands Residencies 3 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 146.7 million; its shares traded at Rs 49, NDB 1 million shares crossed for Rs 112 million; its shares sold at Rs 112, Hemas Holdings 1.7 million shares crossed for Rs 56.1 million; its shares traded at Rs 33, Sunshine Holdings 1.1 million shares crossed for Rs 35.5 million; its shares sold at Rs 32, Vallibel Finance 360,000 shares crossed for Rs 229.4 million; its shares traded at Rs 98 and Access Engineering 300,000 shares crossed to the tune of 22.8 million; its shares sold at Rs 76."
