    "chunk_text": "Access Motors unveils new Range Rover Boutique Residency in Colombo\n\nThe opening of the exclusive Range Rover pop-up at ITC Ratnadipa Colombo One Workplaces (from left): Access Motors Managing Director Theo Fernando, British High Commissioner Andrew Patrick, Access Group Chairman Sumal Perera, Jaguar Land Rover Managing Director \u2013 Asia Pacific Region Garth Turnbull, and former All Blacks Captain Kieran Read \u2013 Pic by Daminda Harsha Perera\n\nStrategically located in Colombo at ITC Ratnadipa Colombo One Workplaces\n\nMarks a milestone in Range Rover\u2019s brand strategy and luxury client engagement\n\nAccess Motors has unveiled a new Range Rover Boutique Residency at ITC Ratnadipa Colombo One Workplaces \u2014 a carefully composed, immersive environment designed as a physical expression of the brand\u2019s modern luxury ethos. Defined by reduction and materiality, the space brings clients closer to the world of Range Rover through considered architecture, curated design elements and a calm, contemporary spatial language.\n\nBuilding on this philosophy, the boutique offers a more intimate, highly personalised client journey. The latest Range Rover vehicles are presented within a refined, contemporary setting, where curated configurations, bespoke options and a dedicated lifestyle selection are explored through a consultative, onetoone approach led by trained specialists.\n\nRange Rover is one of the world\u2019s leading British luxury brands, sold in 121 countries. It belongs to the JLR house of brands together with Defender, Discovery and Jaguar."
