    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "0a91e3d29445d433e1fe356ef4373497",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1747,
    "chunk_text": "AHC Group and AACI strengthen Sri Lanka-Africa ties, driving investment, global collaborations\n\nFrom left: AHC Director \u2013 HR and Admin Duleeka Wakkumbura, Agro Harvest Legal Adviser Dr. Sunil Abeyaratne, AHC Chairman and ICAPIFPO Co-Founder Dr. Nalaka Silva, International Chamber of Agricultural Plantation Industry and Farmer Producer Organisation Founder and Peace Ambassador Dr. H.E.M.N. Sardar Ali, Global India Business Forum Founder and Global President Dr. Jitendra Joshi, CIAC Founder and President and World Peace Diplomacy Organisation Global Founder and President Prof. Dr. G.D. Singh, Asian African Chamber of Commerce and Industry Director General M.J. Puri\n\nAHC Group has entered into a strategic partnership with the Asia Africa Chamber of Commerce and Industry (AACCI) through the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU), marking a significant step towards strengthening international trade and investment ties.\n\nThe agreement was signed recently at the Heritance Hotel in Negombo between AHC Group Chairman, International Chamber of Agricultural Plantation Industry and Farmer Producer Organisation (ICAPIFPO) Co-Founder, and Ambassador of Peace Dr. Nalaka Silva, and AACCI President Dr. G.D. Sing.\n\nThe MoU is expected to facilitate substantial investment inflows into key sectors including agriculture, tourism, imports and exports, real estate, as well as geology and mining. It is also anticipated to generate meaningful employment opportunities, contributing to Sri Lanka\u2019s broader economic growth and development.\n\nSpeaking on the partnership, Dr. Nalaka Silva noted that AHC Group continues to play a pivotal role in advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s agricultural landscape through innovative and sustainable initiatives."
  },
