    "md5": "567b95656ec90b1c5a964675a8df4cf0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1902,
    "chunk_text": "Aitken Spence Elevators and CINEC empower next generation of experts\n\nAitken Spence Elevators, in collaboration with CINEC Campus, recently held the Certificate Awarding Ceremony for the latest batch of trainees of the Elevator Serviceman Course at the Elevator Training Centre (ETC).\n\nThe graduates were awarded their NVQ Level 3 certifications, marking a significant milestone in their professional journey within Sri Lanka\u2019s vertical transportation industry.\n\nThe certification program was developed in partnership with the National Apprentice and Industrial Training Authority (NAITA) and the Vocational Training and Skills Development Ministry, ensuring trainees received industry-recognised qualifications, alongside strong practical competencies. The ceremony was attended by directors of both Aitken Spence and CINEC Campus, as well as staff members, lecturers, and invited guests of the graduating students\n\nAnuka Prashan Pieris, was recognised as the Most Outstanding Student of the batch in appreciation of his exceptional performance and commitment throughout the program. The ETC plays a vital role in addressing the growing demand for skilled elevator service technicians through structured training and hands-on learning. The facility features Sri Lanka\u2019s first Elevator Training Tower, offering trainees practical exposure aligned with both local and international standards.\n\nAll graduates of the current batch have already commenced their careers as technicians and supervisors at Aitken Spence Elevators. Their seamless transition into the workforce reflects the program\u2019s strong emphasis on developing job-ready professionals capable of contributing effectively from day one.\n\nWith further batches planned in the coming months, the ETC continues to strengthen the nation\u2019s skilled workforce, supporting the long-term growth of Sri Lanka\u2019s vertical transportation industry."
  },
