    "md5": "b6db12f0c0ce6564c0506a031c4d8844",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2022,
    "chunk_text": "I was hired as the editorial artist but I always wanted to explore regions that were outside the ambit of an artist\u2019s role in print media. I expressed this desire and following discussions on the matter, the Editor-in-Chief Edmund Ranasinghe, Deputy Editor Dayasena Gunasinghe, and the then Managing Director Leslie Dharmaratne agreed to support me and as importantly accorded me the necessary freedom.\n\nThe \u2018Divaina,\u2019 launched in 1981 revolutionized newspaper art in Sri Lanka. There grew within the general idea of designing an expansive art form. Whereas illustration was generally taken to be a filler of space on a page or, put another way, an insertion that complemented text, \u2018art\u2019 came to do more, i.e. to decorate text but also communicate something more. Among the handful of people who helped \u2018engineer\u2019 this transformation was H A Karunaratne.\n\nOne day Athula Mendis came to me with an interesting piece of information.\n\n\u2018Machang, you have been learning from Stanley Abeysinghe Sir. There\u2019s another great teacher who seems to have noticed you.\u2019\n\n\u2018Something interesting happened today in College. While reading the Divaina paper, he said that there were some really great illustrations in the paper. He said they were different and added that the illustrator cannot be anyone from our college! Now a door has opened. Go see him and see if he would agree to take you on as a student.\u2019\n\nThis is how it began. I went to see \u2018H A Sir\u2019 at his place on Nalandarama Road in Nugegoda. There was a large white wall and a small black door. I knocked. The door opened. A man with a large towel around his waist opened the door. He was tending to a garden with what looked like a thicket of many small trees and a small pond with fish.\n\n\u2018Ah\u2026.are you the one who draws strange kinds of illustrations for the Divaina? Go inside. You can sit. Let me put on a shirt.\u2019\n\nNo one would have thought that this meeting would be the beginning of a unique and fascinating teacher-student relationship."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-02-islandlk-3c3a496b",
