    "chunk_text": "For art to be appreciated people should be able to associate with it closely, so to speak. There are certain preconditions for this to happen. There should be good art galleries. Good art should be exhibited. There should be discussions and debates about art and new trends in art. There should be good art critics. These are not conditions that artists can create. H A Karunaratne did what he could to the best of his ability and strength. He did his duty.\n\nThese are questions that may have troubled the great artist and art teacher H A Karunaratne. He never asked such questions. He is no more. And yet, the colours he obtained from the world around him will continue to fill our minds. We can but enjoy.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
